baseLocus -- compute the locus where a graded module (or O(D) of a Weil divisor) is not globally generated
**********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        I = baseLocus(D)
        I = baseLocus(M)
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note WeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

Given a graded module $M$ with degree 0 global sections $s1, ..., sd$, this
computes the locus where the $si$ do not generate $M$.  Given a Weil divisor
$D$, this computes the base locus of $O(D)$.  For example, consider the rulings
on $P^1 \times P^1$.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,u,v]/ideal(x*y-u*v);|
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor( ideal(x,u) )      |
|                                    |
|o2 = Div(x, u)                      |
|                                    |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R               |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : baseLocus(D)                   |
|                                    |
|o3 = ideal 1                        |
|                                    |
|o3 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+

Next we consider an example of a point on an elliptic curve.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[x,y,z]/ideal(y^2*z-x*(x+z)*(x-z));|
+----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = divisor(ideal(y, x))                 |
|                                              |
|o5 = Div(y, x)                                |
|                                              |
|o5 : WeilDivisor on R                         |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : baseLocus(D)                             |
|                                              |
|o6 = ideal (y, x)                             |
|                                              |
|o6 : Ideal of R                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : baseLocus(2*D)                           |
|                                              |
|o7 = ideal 1                                  |
|                                              |
|o7 : Ideal of R                               |
+----------------------------------------------+

