ceiling(RWeilDivisor) -- produce a WeilDivisor whose coefficients are ceilings or floors of the divisor
*******************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note ceiling: (Macaulay2Doc)ceiling,
  * Usage: 
        ceiling( E1 )
        floor( E1 )
  * Inputs:
      * E1, an instance of the type *note RWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note WeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 

Description
===========

Start with a rational or real Weil divisor.  We form a new divisor whose
coefficients are obtained by applying the ceiling or floor function to them.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z] / ideal(x *y - z^2);                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor({1/2, 4/3}, {ideal(x, z), ideal(y, z)}, CoefficientType =>  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = 4/3*Div(y, z) + 1/2*Div(x, z)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : QWeilDivisor on R                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|QQ)                                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : ceiling( D )                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 2*Div(y, z) + Div(x, z)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : WeilDivisor on R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : floor( D )                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = Div(y, z)                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : WeilDivisor on R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : E = divisor({0.3, -0.7}, {ideal(x, z), ideal(y,z)}, CoefficientType =>  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = -.7*Div(y, z) + .3*Div(x, z)                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : RWeilDivisor on R                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|RR)                                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : ceiling( E )                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = Div(x, z)                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : WeilDivisor on R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : floor( E )                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = -Div(z, y)                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : WeilDivisor on R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note ceiling(RWeilDivisor): ceiling_lpRWeilDivisor_rp, -- produce a
    WeilDivisor whose coefficients are ceilings or floors of the divisor
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in WeilDivisors.m2:2556:0.

