cleanSupport -- removes primes with coefficient zero from a divisor
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        cleanSupport( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 

Description
===========

This function returns a divisor where all entries with coefficient zero are
removed.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor({1,0,-2}, {ideal(x), ideal(y), ideal(z)})|
|                                                          |
|o2 = 0*Div(y) + -2*Div(z) + Div(x)                        |
|                                                          |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : cleanSupport(D)                                      |
|                                                          |
|o3 = -2*Div(z) + Div(x)                                   |
|                                                          |
|o3 : WeilDivisor on R                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

