clearCache -- creates a new divisor with most entries from the cache removed
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        clearCache( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 

Description
===========

This function returns a divisor where the only entries left in the cache is the
key ideals (which points to how the ideals should be displayed to the user).

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor(x);                                |
|                                                    |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                               |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isPrincipal(D)                                 |
|                                                    |
|o3 = true                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : peek (D#cache)                                 |
|                                                    |
|o4 = CacheTable{ideals => MutableHashTable{...1...}}|
|                isPrincipal => {false, true}        |
|                                    1               |
|                divisorToModule => R                |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : E = clearCache(D);                             |
|                                                    |
|o5 : WeilDivisor on R                               |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : peek (E#cache)                                 |
|                                                    |
|o6 = CacheTable{ideals => MutableHashTable{...1...}}|
+----------------------------------------------------+

