coefficient(BasicList,BasicDivisor) -- get the coefficient of an ideal for a fixed divisor
******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note coefficient: (Macaulay2Doc)coefficient,
  * Usage: 
        coefficient(L, D)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, the list of elements
        in a Grobner basis of a height one prime ideal that we want to find the
        coefficient of
      * D, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, the
        divisor in question
  * Outputs:
      * a *note number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, 

Description
===========

This function returns the coefficient of $D$ along the prime divisor generated
by $L$ assuming $L$ is the ordered list of an element

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,u,v]/ideal(x*y-u*v);    |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = divisor(x*u)                   |
|                                        |
|o2 = Div(v, x) + Div(u, y) + 2*Div(u, x)|
|                                        |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : coefficient({u, x}, E)             |
|                                        |
|o3 = 2                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : coefficient({x, u}, E)             |
|                                        |
|o4 = 0                                  |
+----------------------------------------+

