CoefficientType -- an option used to tell divisor construction that a particular type of coefficients are expected.
*******************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

Can be set to ZZ, QQ or RR (or any other Thing) when divisor is called, it
checks whether the coefficient list is a list of instances of this type.  If it
is set to ZZ, QQ or RR then a WeilDivisor, QWeilDivisor or RWeilDivisor are
created.  Default value is ZZ.

Functions with optional argument named CoefficientType:
=======================================================

  * "applyToCoefficients(...,CoefficientType=>...)" -- see *note
    applyToCoefficients: applyToCoefficients, -- apply a function to the
    coefficients of a divisor
  * "divisor(...,CoefficientType=>...)" -- see *note divisor: divisor, --
    constructor for (Weil/Q/R)-divisors

For the programmer
==================

