findElementOfDegree -- find an element of a specified degree
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        findElementOfDegree( n, R )
        findElementOfDegree( l, R )
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * l, a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, 

Description
===========

Given a singly graded ring and an integer $n$, this function tries to find an
element of degree $n$.  If successful, it returns a list with two elements
{$a,b$} such that $a/b$ has degree $n$.  If it is impossible, it gives an
error.  If instead of an integer, you pass it a basic list corresponding to a
multi-degree, it still tries to find $a, b$ in R such that $a/b$ has the
provided multidegree.  It only works on rings with flattened variables (ie, no
Rees algebras). First we do an example without multidegrees.

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/7[x,y,Degrees=>{3, 5}];    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : output = findElementOfDegree(1, R)|
|                                       |
|       2                               |
|o2 = {x , y}                           |
|                                       |
|o2 : List                              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : output#0/output#1                 |
|                                       |
|      2                                |
|     x                                 |
|o3 = --                                |
|      y                                |
|                                       |
|o3 : frac R                            |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : findElementOfDegree(-2, R)        |
|                                       |
|       2   4                           |
|o4 = {y , x }                          |
|                                       |
|o4 : List                              |
+---------------------------------------+

We also do an example with multidegrees

+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x,y,Degrees=>{{1,2}, {3, 5}}];  |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i6 : output = findElementOfDegree({1, 3}, R)|
|                                            |
|       4                                    |
|o6 = {x , y}                                |
|                                            |
|o6 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i7 : output#0/output#1                      |
|                                            |
|      4                                     |
|     x                                      |
|o7 = --                                     |
|      y                                     |
|                                            |
|o7 : frac R                                 |
+--------------------------------------------+

