getLinearDiophantineSolution -- find a solution of the linear Diophantine equation Ax = b
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getLinearDiophantineSolution(l, L)
        getLinearDiophantineSolution(l, A)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, 
      * l, a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, 
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Safe => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        true, turns on or off routine checks in the function
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Given a linear Diophantine equation $Ax = b$ (i.e. an integer matrix with
target vector also integer), we want to find a solution of this equation.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : colList = {{1,3,7}, {2,4,-31}, {1,6,101}, {3,-2,47}, {8,9,1}};|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = transpose matrix colList;                                 |
|                                                                   |
|              3       5                                            |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : b = {1, 2, 3}                                                 |
|                                                                   |
|o3 = {1, 2, 3}                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o3 : List                                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : getLinearDiophantineSolution(b, A)                            |
|                                                                   |
|o4 = {-9268, 3946, 1941, -188, 0}                                  |
|                                                                   |
|o4 : List                                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : sol = getLinearDiophantineSolution(b, colList )               |
|                                                                   |
|o5 = {-9268, 3946, 1941, -188, 0}                                  |
|                                                                   |
|o5 : List                                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : sum apply(#sol, i->(sol#i)*(colList#i) )                      |
|                                                                   |
|o6 = {1, 2, 3}                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o6 : List                                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

When the context is clear, set the Safe option to false in order to avoid
routine checks.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : A = matrix{ {1, 0, 0, 0, 0}, {0, 2, 0, 0, 0}, {3, 4, 5, 6, 8} }|
|                                                                    |
|o7 = | 1 0 0 0 0 |                                                  |
|     | 0 2 0 0 0 |                                                  |
|     | 3 4 5 6 8 |                                                  |
|                                                                    |
|              3       5                                             |
|o7 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : b = {1, 2, 3}                                                  |
|                                                                    |
|o8 = {1, 2, 3}                                                      |
|                                                                    |
|o8 : List                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : getLinearDiophantineSolution(b, A, Safe => false)              |
|                                                                    |
|o9 = {1, 1, 16, -14, 0}                                             |
|                                                                    |
|o9 : List                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note findElementOfDegree: findElementOfDegree, -- find an element of a
    specified degree

