getPrimeCount -- get the number of height-one primes in the support of the divisor
**********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getPrimeCount( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

This function returns the number of height one prime ideals corresponding to
the components of a BasicDivisor.  Note that if you don't call cleanSupport,
this can return primes with coefficient equal to zero.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,u,v]/ideal(x*y-u*v);    |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor(x)                     |
|                                        |
|o2 = Div(v, x) + Div(u, x)              |
|                                        |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : getPrimeCount(D)                   |
|                                        |
|o3 = 2                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : E = divisor(x*u)                   |
|                                        |
|o4 = Div(v, x) + Div(u, y) + 2*Div(u, x)|
|                                        |
|o4 : WeilDivisor on R                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i5 : getPrimeCount(E)                   |
|                                        |
|o5 = 3                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i6 : F = divisor({0}, {ideal(x,u)})     |
|                                        |
|o6 = 0*Div(x, u)                        |
|                                        |
|o6 : WeilDivisor on R                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i7 : getPrimeCount(F)                   |
|                                        |
|o7 = 1                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i8 : getPrimeCount(cleanSupport F)      |
|                                        |
|o8 = 0                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i9 : getPrimeCount(1*F)                 |
|                                        |
|o9 = 0                                  |
+----------------------------------------+

This is equivalent to #primes.

See also
========

  * *note coefficients(BasicDivisor): coefficients_lpBasicDivisor_rp, -- get
    the list of coefficients of a divisor
  * *note gbs: gbs, -- get the list of Groebner bases corresponding to the
    height-one primes in the support of a divisor

Ways to use getPrimeCount:
==========================

  * "getPrimeCount(BasicDivisor)"

