getPrimeDivisors -- get the list of prime divisors of a given divisor
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getPrimeDivisors( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

This function returns the list of prime divisors of a given divisor.  The prime
divisors are all of the class WeilDivisor.  If you do not call cleanSupport,
you may obtain divisors with zero coefficients.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z];                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor({-8, 2, 0}, {ideal(x), ideal(y), ideal(x^2+z)})|
|                                                                |
|o2 = 0*Div(x^2+z) + -8*Div(x) + 2*Div(y)                        |
|                                                                |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : getPrimeDivisors( D )                                      |
|                                                                |
|o3 = {Div(x^2+z), Div(x), Div(y)}                               |
|                                                                |
|o3 : List                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : getPrimeDivisors( cleanSupport D )                         |
|                                                                |
|o4 = {Div(x), Div(y)}                                           |
|                                                                |
|o4 : List                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

