File: WeilDivisors.info, Node: IsGraded, Next: isHomogeneous_lpBasicDivisor_rp, Prev: isEffective, Up: Top

IsGraded -- an option used by numerous functions which tells it to treat the divisors as if we were working on the Proj of the ambient ring.
********************************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

An option used by numerous functions which tells it to treat the divisors as if
we were working on the Proj of the ambient ring.  In other words, setting it to
true tells the function to ignore behavior at the irrelevant ideal (the ideal
generated by vars Ring).  Default value is false.

Functions with optional argument named IsGraded:
================================================

  * "canonicalDivisor(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note canonicalDivisor:
    canonicalDivisor, -- compute a canonical divisor of a ring
  * "divisor(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note divisor: divisor, -- constructor
    for (Weil/Q/R)-divisors
  * "embedAsIdeal(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note embedAsIdeal: embedAsIdeal,
    -- embed a module as an ideal of a ring
  * "isCartier(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note isCartier: isCartier, --
    whether a Weil divisor is Cartier
  * "isLinearEquivalent(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note isLinearEquivalent:
    isLinearEquivalent, -- whether two Weil divisors are linearly equivalent
  * "isPrincipal(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note isPrincipal: isPrincipal, --
    whether a Weil divisor is globally principal
  * "isQCartier(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note isQCartier: isQCartier, --
    whether m times a divisor is Cartier for any m from 1 to a fixed positive
    integer n1.
  * "isQLinearEquivalent(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note isQLinearEquivalent:
    isQLinearEquivalent, -- whether two Q-divisors are linearly equivalent
  * "isSmooth(Ideal,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note isSmooth(Ideal):
    isSmooth_lpIdeal_rp, -- whether R mod the ideal is smooth
  * "isSNC(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note isSNC: isSNC, -- whether the
    divisor is simple normal crossings
  * "nonCartierLocus(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note nonCartierLocus:
    nonCartierLocus, -- the non-Cartier locus of a Weil divisor
  * "ramificationDivisor(...,IsGraded=>...)" -- see *note ramificationDivisor:
    ramificationDivisor, -- compute the ramification divisor of a finite
    inclusion of normal domains or a blowup over a smooth base

For the programmer
==================

The object *note IsGraded: IsGraded, is a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

