isReduced -- whether a divisor is reduced
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        isReduced( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note WeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This function returns true if the divisor is reduced (all coefficients equal to
1), otherwise it returns false.

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z];            |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : D1 = divisor(x^2 * y^3 * z) |
|                                 |
|o2 = 2*Div(x) + 3*Div(y) + Div(z)|
|                                 |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R            |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : D2 = divisor(x * y * z)     |
|                                 |
|o3 = Div(x) + Div(y) + Div(z)    |
|                                 |
|o3 : WeilDivisor on R            |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : isReduced( D1 )             |
|                                 |
|o4 = false                       |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : isReduced( D2 )             |
|                                 |
|o5 = true                        |
+---------------------------------+

