isWellDefined(BasicDivisor) -- whether a divisor is valid
*********************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        isWellDefined( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This function tries to verify that this is a valid divisor.  It checks that the
coefficients are from the right ring (in the
WeilDivisor/QWeilDivisor/RWeilDivisor cases at least).  It also checks to make
sure all the ideals are from the same ring, are prime, and have height one.  If
debugLevel > 0, the function will print an message explaining why the divisor
was not valid.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : debugLevel = 1;                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isWellDefined(divisor({1}, {ideal(x)} ))                           |
|                                                                        |
|o3 = true                                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isWellDefined(divisor({1/2}, {ideal(x)} ))                         |
|(isWellDefined, BasicDivisor): Not all coefficients are integers        |
|                                                                        |
|o4 = false                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isWellDefined(divisor({1/2}, {ideal(x)}, CoefficientType=>QQ))     |
|                                                                        |
|o5 = true                                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isWellDefined(divisor({1}, {ideal(x,y)}))                          |
|(isWellDefined, BasicDivisor): Not all ideals are height one            |
|                                                                        |
|o6 = false                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isWellDefined(divisor({1}, {ideal(x^2)}))                          |
|(isWellDefined, BasicDivisor): Not all ideals are prime                 |
|                                                                        |
|o7 = false                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : S = QQ[a,b];                                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isWellDefined(divisor({1,2}, {ideal(x), ideal(a)}))                |
|(isWellDefined, BasicDivisor): Not all ideals have the same ambient ring|
|                                                                        |
|o9 = false                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note divisor: divisor, -- constructor for (Weil/Q/R)-divisors

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isWellDefined(BasicDivisor): isWellDefined_lpBasicDivisor_rp, --
    whether a divisor is valid
