ring(BasicDivisor) -- get the ambient ring of a divisor
*******************************************************

  * Function: *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)ring,
  * Usage: 
        ring( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

This function returns the ambient ring of a divisor.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z] / ideal(x * y - z^2 );         |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor({1, 2}, {ideal(x, z), ideal(y, z)})|
|                                                    |
|o2 = 2*Div(y, z) + Div(x, z)                        |
|                                                    |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                               |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : ring( D )                                      |
|                                                    |
|o3 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o3 : QuotientRing                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note ring(BasicDivisor): ring_lpBasicDivisor_rp, -- get the ambient ring
    of a divisor
