RWeilDivisor == RWeilDivisor -- whether two divisors are equal
**************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        (D == E)
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note RWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
      * E, an instance of the type *note RWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This function returns true if the two divisors are equal

+----------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];     |
+----------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor(x*y);|
|                      |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R |
+----------------------+
|i3 : E = divisor(x);  |
|                      |
|o3 : WeilDivisor on R |
+----------------------+
|i4 : F = divisor(y);  |
|                      |
|o4 : WeilDivisor on R |
+----------------------+
|i5 : D == E           |
|                      |
|o5 = false            |
+----------------------+
|i6 : D == E+F         |
|                      |
|o6 = true             |
+----------------------+

Here is an example with rational coefficients compared with integer
coefficients.

+-------------------------+
|i7 : R = QQ[x,y];        |
+-------------------------+
|i8 : D = (1/2)*divisor(x)|
|                         |
|o8 = 1/2*Div(x)          |
|                         |
|o8 : QWeilDivisor on R   |
+-------------------------+
|i9 : D == 2*D            |
|                         |
|o9 = false               |
+-------------------------+
|i10 : D + D == 2*D       |
|                         |
|o10 = true               |
+-------------------------+
|i11 : E = divisor(x)     |
|                         |
|o11 = Div(x)             |
|                         |
|o11 : WeilDivisor on R   |
+-------------------------+
|i12 : D == E             |
|                         |
|o12 = false              |
+-------------------------+
|i13 : 2*D == E           |
|                         |
|o13 = true               |
+-------------------------+

