toQWeilDivisor -- create a Q-Weil divisor from a Weil divisor
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        toQWeilDivisor( D )
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note QWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note QWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 

Description
===========

Turn a Weil divisor into a Q-divisor (or do nothing to a Q-divisor).

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/5[x, y];                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor(x);                                          |
|                                                              |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = toQWeilDivisor(D)                                    |
|                                                              |
|o3 = Div(x)                                                   |
|                                                              |
|o3 : QWeilDivisor on R                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : toQWeilDivisor(E)                                        |
|                                                              |
|o4 = Div(x)                                                   |
|                                                              |
|o4 : QWeilDivisor on R                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = divisor({3, 0, -2}, {ideal(x), ideal(y), ideal(x+y)})|
|                                                              |
|o5 = -2*Div(x+y) + 3*Div(x) + 0*Div(y)                        |
|                                                              |
|o5 : WeilDivisor on R                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note toWeilDivisor: toWeilDivisor, -- create a Weil divisor from a Q or
    R-divisor
