toRWeilDivisor -- create a R-divisor from a Q or Weil divisor
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        toRWeilDivisor( D1 )
        toRWeilDivisor( E1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note WeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
      * E1, an instance of the type *note QWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
      * E1, an instance of the type *note RWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note RWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 

Description
===========

Turn a Weil divisor or a Q-divisor into a R-divisor (or do nothing to a
R-divisor).

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/5[x,y];                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor({2, 0, -4}, {ideal(x), ideal(y), ideal(x-y)})|
|                                                              |
|o2 = -4*Div(x-y) + 2*Div(x) + 0*Div(y)                        |
|                                                              |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = (1/2)*D                                              |
|                                                              |
|o3 = -2*Div(x-y) + Div(x)                                     |
|                                                              |
|o3 : QWeilDivisor on R                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : F = toRWeilDivisor(D)                                    |
|                                                              |
|o4 = -4*Div(x-y) + 2*Div(x)                                   |
|                                                              |
|o4 : RWeilDivisor on R                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : G = toRWeilDivisor(E)                                    |
|                                                              |
|o5 = -2*Div(x-y) + Div(x)                                     |
|                                                              |
|o5 : RWeilDivisor on R                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : F == 2*G                                                 |
|                                                              |
|o6 = true                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note toWeilDivisor: toWeilDivisor, -- create a Weil divisor from a Q or
    R-divisor
  * *note toQWeilDivisor: toQWeilDivisor, -- create a Q-Weil divisor from a
    Weil divisor

