toWeilDivisor -- create a Weil divisor from a Q or R-divisor
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        toWeilDivisor( E1 )
  * Inputs:
      * E1, an instance of the type *note RWeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note WeilDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 

Description
===========

Given a divisor with rational or real coefficients, but whose coefficients are
actually integers, we first check if all coefficients are integers. If so we
make this Weil divisor.  Otherwise, an error is thrown.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x];                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D=divisor({3/2}, {ideal(x)}, CoefficientType=>QQ)                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = 3/2*Div(x)                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : QWeilDivisor on R                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E=divisor({1.5}, {ideal(x)}, CoefficientType=>RR)                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 1.5*Div(x)                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : RWeilDivisor on R                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : toWeilDivisor(2*D)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 3*Div(x)                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : WeilDivisor on R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : toWeilDivisor(2*E)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 3*Div(x)                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : WeilDivisor on R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isWeilDivisor(D)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : try toWeilDivisor(D) then print "converted to a WeilDivisor" else print |
|can't be converted to a WeilDivisor                                          |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|"can't be converted to a WeilDivisor"                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Notice in the final computation, D cannot be converted into a Weil divisor
since $D$ has non-integer coefficients, but 2*D can be converted into a Weil
divisor.

See also
========

  * *note toQWeilDivisor: toQWeilDivisor, -- create a Q-Weil divisor from a
    Weil divisor
  * *note toRWeilDivisor: toRWeilDivisor, -- create a R-divisor from a Q or
    Weil divisor
  * *note isWeilDivisor: isWeilDivisor, -- whether a rational/real divisor is
    in actuality a Weil divisor

Ways to use toWeilDivisor:
==========================

  * "toWeilDivisor(RWeilDivisor)"

