trim(BasicDivisor) -- trims the ideals displayed to the user and removes primes with coefficient zero
*****************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note trim: (Macaulay2Doc)trim,
  * Usage: 
        trim( D1 )
  * Inputs:
      * D1, an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)Complement, => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note BasicDivisor: BasicDivisor,, 

Description
===========

This function returns a divisor where all entries with coefficient zero are
removed and where the ideals displayed to the user are trimmed.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]/ideal(x*y-z^2);                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = divisor({1,0,-2}, {ideal(x, z), ideal(x-z,y-z), ideal(y+z, z)});|
|                                                                         |
|o2 : WeilDivisor on R                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : cleanSupport(D)                                                     |
|                                                                         |
|o3 = Div(x, z) + -2*Div(y+z, z)                                          |
|                                                                         |
|o3 : WeilDivisor on R                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : trim(D)                                                             |
|                                                                         |
|o4 = Div(z, x) + -2*Div(z, y)                                            |
|                                                                         |
|o4 : WeilDivisor on R                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D == trim(D)                                                        |
|                                                                         |
|o5 = true                                                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note trim(BasicDivisor): trim_lpBasicDivisor_rp, -- trims the ideals
    displayed to the user and removes primes with coefficient zero
